{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789910011,"nonce":"9DlyDLqmD8tBoE6SxefB03RzHqs=","message":"Fixed in e1dd9c2cd61252d4b13a0ad57f1315da09f98232. bind_foreign_method_fn is consulted per foreign method (module, class, is_static, signature) before the #!native route, binding a NativeFn on the class; unbound methods fall through to dlopen as before, and the no-#!native warning only fires for what nothing bound. bind_foreign_class_fn was removed: this runtime has no allocate/finalize step for foreign classes (plugins create ObjForeign values from their own factory methods), so the callback had nothing to hook; the C WrenConfiguration keeps both slots for layout compatibility, marked not read. The related alias bug is fixed in the same commit: import \"m\" for A as B now binds B to m's A (the resolver records the exported name in the import source, wlbc bumped to v8 with a v7 reader, AOT bootstrap copies by the exported name too). e2e tests cover both.","files":null}]}